{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1156835-new-horror-mister-switch","id":1156835,"title":"[New Horror] Mister Switch","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-07T16:44:53-08:00","id":1156835,"title":"[New Horror] Mister Switch","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">In the 21<sup>st</sup> century, people\u2019s lives are being so influenced by digital technology that new hopes and fears surrounding it have taken hold in the zeitgeist. We are afraid of the loss of our privacy, but at the same time we have a strange reverence for those who can use this technology to its full potential. This enormous mythical resonance has coalesced in the form of an entity embodying the best and worst aspects of the hacker archetype: a surreal and elusive gremlin called Mister Switch.<br /> <br /> This entity has no home, for it doesn\u2019t need any. It lives either within ones and zeroes or blending into the streets, looking for opportunities to test its hacking skills and miraculous powers. While it will readily jump to defend those who convince it they have been victims of injustice, especially the digital kind, he is also an incorrigible thief and liar. One can never be completely sure if he has one\u2019s best interests in mind, and that does not seem to bother him. He enjoys the thrill of the chase and infiltration first and foremost, but does not begrudge those who manage to outsmart him. He tends to find such individuals fascinating, and tries to find out all he can about them in order to come up with more \u201cfun\u201d mind games for them.<br /> <br /> The key to confronting Mister Switch, besides taking advantage of his Bans, is to goad him into thinking he is smarter than you. He has a bad habit of assuming that getting what he wants will be easy, and when someone plays dumb or the victim, he is likely to buy it since it feeds his ego. Furthermore, despite being a master at covering his tracks, he loves to spend his dirty money on frivolous, extravagant and whimsical things, just to say he owns them for a moment. He will never drive ordinary cars or wear bargain bin clothes, and that can be used to reveal him. Finally, he is a bit of a coward and avoids combat whenever possible, despite having the power to easily electrocute people to death or cause major disasters. He will likely panic if threatened with violence, and that can be used in conjunction with his Bans to trap and banish him.<br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> In his true form, Mister Switch looks like a Daft Punk member, with a glass dome covering an electronic brain where the top of its head should be. It has a hologram projector for a face that can assume any image, and a voice modulator that makes him sound constantly hyped up and ready to start trouble. To top it all off, he wears a TRON-style outfit consisting of trench coat, gloves and boots that looks like something from a cyberpunk movie. <br /> <br /> <b>Virtue: </b>Justice<br /> <b>Vice: </b>Greed/Mischief<br /> <b>Aspirations: </b>Challenge And Expose Authorities And Wrong-Doers, Leave Calling Cards, Collect Sensitive And Well Guarded Information<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 5, Wits 7, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 4, Dexterity 6, Stamina 6<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 5, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 1, Crafts 2, Computer (Hacking, Hiding Footprints) 5, Investigation 3, Occult 1, Athletics 3, Brawl 1, Firearms 2, Larceny (Security Systems) 4, Stealth 3, Empathy 1, Expression (Wisecracking) 2, Persuasion 3, Streetwise 2, Subterfuge (Mind Games, Long Cons) 3<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area Of Expertise 1 (Mind Games), Eidetic Memory 2, Interdisciplinary Specialty 1 (Mind Games), Professional Training 5 (Gremlin: Computer, Larceny, Subterfuge), Vice-Ridden 2, Double Jointed 2, Parkour 4, Sleight Of Hand 2, Anonymity 5, Closed Book 3, Contacts (Hackers, Vigilantes), Iron Will 2, Resources 4, Untouchable 1<br /> <br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 14<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 9<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 9<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 20<br /> <b>Health:</b> 11<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 6<br /> <br /> <b>Ban:</b> Must always travel within five yards of an electronic device<br /> <br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot enter locations without electric power<br /> <br /> <b>Ban:</b> Must appear if someone leaves a signal for him in an area with sensitive information<br /> <br /> <b>Ban:</b> Publishing a photo of his real form on the Internet banishes him for a year and a day.<br /> <br /> <b>Ban:</b> Can only use Numina and Psychic Talent while in possession of a functional wrist-mounted device.<br /> <br /> <b>Dread Powers: </b>Gremlin, Influence (Computers 3, Mischief 1), Numen (Hallucination, Mortal Mask, Seek, Teleportation*), Psychic Talent* x 3 (Technopathy 2, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760764-which-supernatural-style-comes-next?p=1131153#post1131153\"><b>Antennae Mind 5</b></a>, Psychokinesis 5/<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/842864-advanced-supernatural-merits-and-styled-supernatural-merits\"><b>Advanced 4/Epic 2</b></a> [Electricity]), Surprise Entrance, Price Of Power x 5<br /> <br /> <b>*Teleportation:</b> When the entity moves, it may reflexively spend 1 Essence to vanish and reappear at another location within its line of sight up to its (Rank x Speed) in yards away. Doing so adds +2 to its Defense for the turn. If the entity has the Seek Numen, it may teleport to the nearest location with a suitable Condition by spending 3 Essence. The entity can spend an additional 2 points of Essence to take a passenger with them (an unwilling passage may resist with a roll of Resolve + Composure + Supernatural Tolerance).<br /> <br /> <b>*Psychic Talent: </b>Creatures with this dread power are endowed with great powers of the mind. Each dot in this Dread Power grants a creature a number of Merit dots equal to its Potency. These Merit dots may be used to purchase Supernatural Merits.<br /> <br /> <b>*Price Of Power:</b> By taking on an additional Ban or Bane, an entity can increase its repertoire of abilities. Each additional Ban or Bane can give it one of the following.<br /> <br /> * Two Numina, Influence dots, or Manifestations.<br /> * An increase of its maximum Essence pool by 5.<br /> * A Dread Power.<br /> <br /> An entity may take this Numina a number of times equal to its Rank.<br /> <br /> <b>Note:</b> Mister Switch uses Computer instead of Occult for Dread Powers.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-